  "notes": "The Hypnotize record with a sung layer on it. The research frames the Oscar-winning song as a \"crunk-style pimp rap composition\" — a static minor vamp with a **sung female counter-hook over it** — and calls that split (\"hard beat, sung hook\") the template the *Hustle & Flow* songs made. So the distinctive block here is `countermelody`: a high `densityRatio`, a +12 offset so it sits above the ostinato rather than under it, and `fillGapsOnly` **off**, because a sung counter-hook runs across the loop instead of hiding in its gaps. That is the opposite setting from every other classic-era entry in this batch. Under it, the beat is the crunk-era board: 16th cowbell at 4–7 a bar and roll-driven transitions, which is what the perc block and the mid-ramp snare roll author. The melodic layer is a piano/organ ostinato, so `timbreHint` is `church_organ` against the piano and bell entries around it. Harmony is a static minor vamp with `impliedByRiff` set; the i–VI and i–VII families carry a third of the drone's weight between them. ⚠ `medium`: the research rates it medium — chart data, the Oscar credit and the crunk-composition description are sourced, but **the drums and tempo are inherited from the board** (70–82 half-time = 140–164 straight, marked [LOW-CONF]), so `session.bpm`, `drums.kick` and `drums.snare` are the inferred ones. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 40 to 39 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 40 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts. ⚠ `countermelody.fillGapsOnly` returned to true. With it off and a density of 0.6, the counter plays THROUGH the melody rather than around it, and coherence.rs measures that as the counter sounding the melody own pitch at the same moment — a second lead rather than an answer. The register offset and the styles are untouched; what changed is that it waits its turn.",
